[21:47:39] 💭 The problem: `Makefile.variables` computes `ROOTDIR ?= $(shell git rev-parse --show-toplevel)`. Since hideGit=true masks the .git (it appears as a character device), `git rev-parse` fails → ROOTDIR is empty → `Makefile.env` includes `/common.env` (empty ROOTDIR + `/common.env`) which doesn't exist.

This is the known hideGit issue. The CLAUDE.md says: "When hideGit=true active, GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false is typically already set in the container environment, so go test, errcheck, gosec, golangci-li…
[21:47:39] `make` fails at the Makefile level because `ROOTDIR` is derived from `git rev-parse`, which hideGit masks. The `?=` allows overriding. Let me check the setup and try with an explicit ROOTDIR.


[21:47:39] $ cat .dark-factory.yaml 2>/dev/null | head -40; echo "=== Makefile.docker ROOTDIR usage ==="; grep -n "ROOTDIR" Makefile.docker Makefile.precommit Makefile.variables Makefile.env 2>/dev/null
